From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:02:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wbemdisp: Name the scripting objects' classes, and tell a
 script why a call failed, as Windows does.

Measured on Windows 11 build 29671 with tools/winmgmtsprobe (classinfo.c,
errorinfo.c, errors.vbs):

- Every object answers IProvideClassInfo with its class (SWbemLocator,
  SWbemServicesEx, SWbemObjectEx, SWbemNamedValue, ...), which is what
  VBScript's TypeName prints; the classes are in the type library.
- A connection is an ISWbemServicesEx: Put (DISPID 20) puts an instance
  and gives its path, PutAsync (21) is a stub.
- A failed call tells the script the status's text, its line break a
  space, and the class that failed it.
- A query asked to return at once (the default) fails when its results
  are asked for, with no text; an object set's Item finds an object by
  its relative or full path, and its Security_ is its own.
- WbemScripting.SWbemLastError can be created when there is a last
  error; there never is one here, which is E_FAIL.

The test checks the classes, the errors and the queries; on Windows it
has no failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

